1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,454
A smoother opening price can still give early buyers more tokens.

2
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:06,773
Measure both before launch.

3
00:00:06,773 --> 00:00:11,797
This is a local validator, synthetic Xerox tokens, and a test signer.

4
00:00:12,966 --> 00:00:17,487
Same supply, opening price, reserve threshold, and fees.

5
00:00:17,437 --> 00:00:23,377
The long curve lowers the first price jump from three hundred eleven to two hundred thirty nine percent.

6
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:28,830
But early buyers receive two point five three percentage points more of total buy output.

7
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:31,449
Choose with both results visible.

8
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:34,630
Now selling pressure.

9
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:38,699
The opening buyer sells half, then retail buyers enter.

10
00:00:38,699 --> 00:00:42,854
Each trade updates reserves, fees, and inventory.

11
00:00:42,854 --> 00:00:46,449
Compare how much buying restores the pre sale price.

12
00:00:46,449 --> 00:00:48,985
Neither curve graduates here.

13
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:53,508
Export the integer ledger and visual summary.

14
00:00:53,458 --> 00:00:55,613
Select the long curve.

15
00:00:55,613 --> 00:01:01,435
The transaction builder receives that exact configuration, also preserved in the share link.

16
00:01:02,599 --> 00:01:04,965
Check the cost before signing.

17
00:01:04,915 --> 00:01:08,118
This long curve needs two transactions.

18
00:01:08,118 --> 00:01:12,808
The configuration succeeds; we deliberately decline token creation.

19
00:01:13,998 --> 00:01:15,900
Reload the page.

20
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:19,874
The saved transaction reference finds the paid configuration.

21
00:01:19,874 --> 00:01:22,707
Check the remaining cost without signing.

22
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:27,064
Token creation uses a new mint address, shown before approval.

23
00:01:27,064 --> 00:01:30,386
Finish once, reusing the original curve.

24
00:01:30,386 --> 00:01:34,683
The recording checks it against the selected scenario configuration.

25
00:01:35,865 --> 00:01:38,065
Read wallet balances.

26
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:42,015
Quote a small buy, review minimum output, then sign.

27
00:01:42,015 --> 00:01:46,288
The refreshed token accounts show more base tokens and less quote.

28
00:01:47,464 --> 00:01:51,080
Use half my token balance fills the exact amount.

29
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:53,566
Review minimum output and sell.

30
00:01:53,566 --> 00:01:57,435
Base tokens decrease; the quote balance increases.

31
00:01:58,597 --> 00:02:02,189
A further buy reaches graduation with a partial fill.

32
00:02:02,139 --> 00:02:06,485
Review migration cost, then create the DAMM version two pool.

33
00:02:06,485 --> 00:02:09,544
Read both destination vault balances.

34
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:18,310
Fifty six swaps across eight local pools checked both curves, SOL and Xerox, and fixed and declining fees.

35
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:24,820
Predicted raw prices, reserves, fees, inventory, and quote transfers matched execution.

36
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:27,713
Data and hashes are in the repository.

37
00:02:28,897 --> 00:02:32,668
Scenarios expose trade offs, not forecasts.

38
00:02:32,618 --> 00:02:36,916
External quote liquidity and stock price changes are not modeled.

39
00:02:36,916 --> 00:02:42,511
Real Phantom execution, mainnet transactions, and builder trials remain open.

40
00:02:42,511 --> 00:02:45,547
Try the product and inspect the evidence.
